Client-Side Routing
Definition
Client-Side Routing means navigation happens inside the browser without requesting a new page from the server.

React Router uses Client-Side Routing.
Advantages
Very Fast
No page reload
Better user experience
Less server requests

Disadvantages
Initial bundle size is larger.
JavaScript must load before the app works.


Server-Side Routing
Definition
Server-Side Routing means every page request goes to the server.

The server sends a new HTML page every time.
Advantages
Good SEO
Initial page loads with HTML.
Works even if JavaScript is disabled (depending on the application).

Disadvantages
Slower navigation
Page refresh every time
More server requests



